{{PROJECT_NAME}} — Licence overview

This repository is a **parts library**: a record of components that other
companies design, make and sell. We did not design anything in it.

That makes its licensing different from a machine repository, and the
difference is the whole point of this file. Two kinds of content live here.

## The record we compile — CC BY-SA 4.0

Applies to: [`bom/`](bom/) part tables, the `okh.toml` manifests, our own
notes under `docs/`, this file, README and other text written by this project.

Part numbers, dimensions, masses and the specifications we write down are facts
we gathered and organised ourselves. They are not a copy of anyone's catalogue.

Full text: [`LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt)

## Supplier files — their own terms, not ours

Applies to: everything under any `cad/` directory, and every
`docs/datasheets/` directory.

These are geometry files and datasheets belonging to the brands that make the
parts, together with the FreeCAD documents we build from them. A document built
from a supplier's model is derived from their work, so it sits on their side of
this line. **None of it is covered by the licence above.**

Each brand records its own download terms in the `[brand]` table of its
`okh.toml`. A file is committed only where those terms allow it. Everything
else is recorded as `fetch-only`: the address, the checksum and the date are
committed, and each person downloads it from the brand under the brand's terms.

## Nothing here is hardware we designed

There is deliberately no CERN Open Hardware Licence in this repository. Writing
one over a supplier's file would claim a licence on something we do not own.

## Directory-level pointers

Each content directory also carries a short `LICENSE` file restating which of
the above applies to it.

## Trademarks

The {{ORGANISATION}} name and logo are trademarks and are not covered by the
licence above. Brand names and part numbers recorded in this repository are the
trademarks of the companies that own them, used here to identify their parts.
See [`TRADEMARKS.md`](TRADEMARKS.md).
